{"name":"Freesia","hex":"#f3c12c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Freesia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Iridaceae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Freesia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Freesia","blocks":[{"text":"Freesia is a genus of herbaceous perennial flowering plants in the family Iridaceae, first described as a genus in 1866 by Christian Friedrich Ecklon (1886) and named after the German botanist and medical practitioner, Friedrich Freese (1795–1876). It is native to the eastern side of southern Africa, from Kenya south to South Africa, most species being found in Cape Provinces. Species of the former genus Anomatheca are now included in Freesia. The plants commonly known as \"freesias\", with fragrant funnel-shaped flowers, are cultivated hybrids of a number of Freesia species. Some other species are also grown as ornamental plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Freesia.jpg/330px-Freesia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freesia"},{"title":"Freesia (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Freesia  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Jiro Matsumoto. It was serialized in Shogakukan's seinen manga magazine Monthly Ikki between September 2001 and August 2009, with its chapters collected in 12 tankōbon volumes. A live-action film adaptation was released in February 2007."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Freesia_%28manga%29_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freesia_(manga)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg/120px-Freesia_refracta_%28Jacq.%29_Klatt_%28AM_AK333551-2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna